WEBVTT

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:28.862
Coming this fall...

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:31.198
Some cops can read minds.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:33.742
Did you do it or not?
I'm not a mind reader.

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:36.161
Some cops can see the past.

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:39.581
I could solve this crime if only
I had personally watched it happen.

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:42.459
And some cops get help from angels.

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:45.254
Come on, Gabriel,
you must have seen something!

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:48.173
Nah, man, I ain't seen nothing for no cop.

00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:54.847
But there's still one cop
with no special abilitieswhatsoever.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.975
Ah, there's only one way to know
who committed this crime.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.811
I'll just have to find out.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:05.357
Detective Klaus Mandela is
the Finder Outer.

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:08.944
This truly is
the golden age of television.

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:11.655
Hey, Papa, want to help me
earn a merit badge?

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.115
Hmm? Sorry, son.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.784
Right now,
NBC needs my love more than you do.

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:19.037
Lrrr!

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:22.583
Either help the boy,
or go outside and degauss the lawn!

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:24.209
Oh, very well.

00:01:27.379 --> 00:01:28.422
Merit badges.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:29.756
Ah, this brings me back.

00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:31.884
Oh, Bone Whittling.

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:33.218
I used to love that.

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.262
Patricide.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:36.930
Well, let's work up to that one.

00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:38.390
How about Skull Arranging?

00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:40.475
That is for Grrrl Scouts!

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:43.312
Men bring the skulls home,
women arrange them.

00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:45.814
I'm gonna help you earn a manly badge.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:47.357
Planetary Invasion!

00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:50.402
But that's really hard.

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:51.862
Hard shmard.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:55.157
I'll let you invade the easiest planet
in the whole galaxy.

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:59.077
Good news, everyone!

00:01:59.161 --> 00:02:01.205
I'm in terrible pain.

00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:03.707
- How is that good news?
- It's not.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.336
I've run out of Good News brand
herbal supplement.

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:10.297
If you don't get me
more Good News, everyone,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.927
my arthritis will make me seize up
like a dried monkey carcass.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:16.303
I've seen those.

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:17.888
In the Great Monkey Desert.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:23.435
We interrupt your TV being off
for this special bulletin.

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:26.855
An alien saucer has been detected
en route to Earth.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:31.401
We now go live to the White House lawn,
where such things usually land.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.206
Go on. Ring the bell and invade them.

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:47.793
Yes?

00:02:47.876 --> 00:02:49.378
Um, hi?

00:02:49.461 --> 00:02:53.131
I... I'm Jrrr,
of the planet Omicron Persei 8.

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:55.425
Uh, what's that? Speak up, son.

00:02:56.134 --> 00:02:58.512
Don't look at me. You're invading him.

00:02:58.595 --> 00:03:03.100
I just wanted to know...
Well, I'm here to invade your planet?

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:08.063
Oh, what a cute little...

00:03:10.065 --> 00:03:11.066
Uh-oh.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:16.071
Brannigan! Get out here and surrender
before I get my expletives deleted!

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:20.868
And Earth is yours.

00:03:21.051 --> 00:03:23.387
So, sire, how may I please you?

00:03:23.929 --> 00:03:25.013
Go ahead.

00:03:25.097 --> 00:03:27.224
His bowels aren't gonna disem themselves.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.809
Can't we just go?

00:03:28.892 --> 00:03:31.061
Mmm-mmm. Not until you blow something up.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.521
Aw, man.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.446
Uh, uh...

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.198
Just pick something and blow it up

00:03:43.282 --> 00:03:45.659
so I can get home in time
for The Finder Outer.

00:03:45.742 --> 00:03:46.743
Oh...

00:03:49.997 --> 00:03:51.248
What the...

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.166
All right, good enough. Let's go.

00:03:59.798 --> 00:04:02.467
He killed my second-to-last Agnew.

00:04:02.551 --> 00:04:05.762
Rose Mary! Sweep the booze bottles
off my desk!

00:04:05.846 --> 00:04:07.848
I'm addressing the planet.

00:04:07.931 --> 00:04:09.391
First, brush your teeth!

00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:10.642
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:13.312
My fellow Earthicans,

00:04:13.395 --> 00:04:16.732
a great American monster
has been silenced.

00:04:16.815 --> 00:04:18.734
Clone of Agnew is gone,

00:04:18.817 --> 00:04:22.654
killed in his clubbing shoes
by ruthless Omicronians.

00:04:22.738 --> 00:04:25.073
But we're gonna get even, by golly.

00:04:25.782 --> 00:04:28.035
Aw, crap, he's on every channel!

00:04:28.118 --> 00:04:29.536
Effective immediately,

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:35.083
I'm calling fora planetary embargo
against Omicron Persei 8.

00:04:35.792 --> 00:04:37.169
Where's my Hot in Cleveland?

00:04:37.252 --> 00:04:40.047
All trade with the Omicronians
stops today.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.341
And that includes cultural exports.

00:04:42.424 --> 00:04:43.425
Cultural?

00:04:43.508 --> 00:04:45.218
I'm talking about TV!

00:04:45.302 --> 00:04:46.345
Nixon out!

00:04:49.473 --> 00:04:54.019
No!

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:01.350
Well, I never liked going
to Omicron Persei 8 anyway.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.320
If we want to breathe sulfuric acid

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.572
and get our heads torn off
by giant lizards,

00:05:05.656 --> 00:05:07.532
we can always go to Gary, Indiana.

00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:11.328
Even I would never send you
to Gary, Indiana.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:14.247
But I am sending you to Omicron Persei 8.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:17.167
Oh, my gosh, are you kidding?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:21.546
You see, the active ingredient
in my Good News herbal supplement

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.424
grows only on Omicron Persei 8.

00:05:24.508 --> 00:05:26.051
And due to the embargo,

00:05:26.134 --> 00:05:29.262
the only place to get it
is straight from the source.

00:05:29.346 --> 00:05:31.598
The deadly, deadly source.

00:05:31.682 --> 00:05:34.685
I will not endanger this crew
for some quack remedy.

00:05:34.768 --> 00:05:38.981
Ha! The Sacred Weed of Omicron
is a serious herb.

00:05:39.064 --> 00:05:40.565
Sacred Weed you say?

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:46.405
Sweet toke of Ocracoke,
this stuff's the Omichronic!

00:05:46.488 --> 00:05:47.614
To the ship!

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.414
We can't get through.
The planet's blockaded.

00:05:55.497 --> 00:05:58.625
That won't stop us.
Activate cloaking device.

00:05:58.709 --> 00:06:00.043
There's no such thing.

00:06:00.127 --> 00:06:02.254
Then, engage deflector shields.

00:06:02.337 --> 00:06:04.131
That's from TV, Geordi.

00:06:04.214 --> 00:06:06.758
Well, what sort of stealth technology
do we have?

00:06:06.842 --> 00:06:08.010
A can of paint.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.559
Sir, there's an Omicronian ship
requesting safe passage home.

00:06:15.642 --> 00:06:17.561
Home, eh? That's where I live.

00:06:17.644 --> 00:06:19.354
Let them through the blockade.

00:06:25.944 --> 00:06:28.947
Okay, buddy up
and look out for Omicronians.

00:06:29.031 --> 00:06:31.825
It's up to everyone
to get their partner back alive.

00:06:31.908 --> 00:06:33.535
Fry, you go with Bender.

00:06:33.619 --> 00:06:34.911
Amy, with Leela.

00:06:34.995 --> 00:06:36.580
And I'll go with...

00:06:37.372 --> 00:06:39.458
Screwed again, my friend.

00:06:44.338 --> 00:06:46.548
Hey, Bender, you better check your ass.

00:06:46.632 --> 00:06:48.383
I think it's leaking enchantment.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:51.219
That's not enchantment, it's the herbs!

00:06:51.303 --> 00:06:54.514
Bender's electric field
is activating their bioluminescence.

00:06:54.598 --> 00:06:56.266
Whoa!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.352
We'll need scientific samples.

00:06:58.435 --> 00:07:00.896
Everyone, start filling these dime bags.

00:07:07.945 --> 00:07:09.655
Whoa, a palace!

00:07:09.738 --> 00:07:11.573
Parapets, battlements,

00:07:11.657 --> 00:07:14.201
everything my
Big Book of Castles promised.

00:07:14.284 --> 00:07:15.702
I'm gonna sneak a closer look.

00:07:15.786 --> 00:07:18.372
Bender, you'll let me know
if we have to cheese it, right?

00:07:18.455 --> 00:07:20.248
First Law of Robotics, baby.

00:07:29.591 --> 00:07:31.093
Five-O, five-O!

00:07:31.176 --> 00:07:32.177
Five what?

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.512
Five Omicronians!

00:07:33.595 --> 00:07:35.806
Everyone, grab your buddy
and get back to the ship!

00:07:39.101 --> 00:07:40.102
Coming through!

00:07:41.478 --> 00:07:42.604
Is everyone on board?

00:07:42.688 --> 00:07:43.939
I got my buddy.

00:07:44.022 --> 00:07:45.274
Hermes is my buddy.

00:07:45.357 --> 00:07:47.276
Bender, where's Fry?

00:07:47.359 --> 00:07:49.236
I saw him in the, uh, kitchen.

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:50.487
With Dinah.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.365
You know,
the dyno-matic food-service robot.

00:07:53.448 --> 00:07:54.449
Let's go already!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.792
I smell the stink of Earth humans.
Fan out!

00:08:06.795 --> 00:08:08.797
They got away, Your Scaliness.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.674
We must have just missed them.

00:08:10.757 --> 00:08:12.718
The ground is still warm.

00:08:22.394 --> 00:08:24.646
I want my Earth shows!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.024
These local programs
are completely unwatchable.

00:08:31.278 --> 00:08:33.280
Hey, Pops, want to play skull ball?

00:08:33.363 --> 00:08:35.365
I'm watching something here.

00:08:43.582 --> 00:08:45.459
Hello?

00:08:48.378 --> 00:08:49.379
Ow!

00:08:52.007 --> 00:08:54.384
Uh, y... you can come out.

00:08:54.843 --> 00:08:56.303
Don't be s... scared.

00:09:05.312 --> 00:09:06.730
Mmm.

00:09:18.909 --> 00:09:19.910
You're an alien?

00:09:19.993 --> 00:09:21.620
Do you speak English?

00:09:21.703 --> 00:09:23.789
English?

00:09:23.872 --> 00:09:27.000
You must be a terrestrial
from that Earth ship they were hunting.

00:09:27.084 --> 00:09:28.961
Don't worry, I won't hurt you.

00:09:29.044 --> 00:09:30.087
Hey, thanks.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.254
You want some candy?

00:09:31.338 --> 00:09:34.132
Ew. You were eating my turds?

00:09:34.216 --> 00:09:35.509
Feces pieces?

00:09:35.592 --> 00:09:36.635
Blech!

00:09:36.718 --> 00:09:38.053
You must be hungry.

00:09:38.136 --> 00:09:39.179
Really hungry.

00:09:39.262 --> 00:09:40.764
Come inside, I'll feed you.

00:09:40.847 --> 00:09:43.100
Okay, but I'm kind of picky.

00:09:44.643 --> 00:09:46.144
I'm gonna call you "T."

00:09:46.228 --> 00:09:47.312
For terrestrial?

00:09:47.396 --> 00:09:49.022
No, "Turd-eater."

00:09:49.106 --> 00:09:50.857
But I have to hide you from my dad.

00:09:50.941 --> 00:09:52.734
He's really mad at humans

00:09:52.818 --> 00:09:55.070
'cause he can't
watch television.

00:09:55.153 --> 00:09:57.030
Your dad must be Lrrr!

00:09:57.114 --> 00:10:00.575
"Ruler of the planet
Omicron Persei 8."

00:10:02.869 --> 00:10:04.496
He's a terrible father.

00:10:07.874 --> 00:10:09.793
Bender, do you know where Fry is?

00:10:09.876 --> 00:10:13.380
I haven't seen him since we got back
from Omicron Persei 8.

00:10:13.463 --> 00:10:16.091
Fry? Uh, you just missed him.

00:10:16.174 --> 00:10:17.801
He went out to buy you flowers.

00:10:17.884 --> 00:10:19.386
Whatever kind you like best.

00:10:19.469 --> 00:10:20.846
'Cause he loves you and crap.

00:10:20.929 --> 00:10:23.140
Aw, that's so sweet.

00:10:23.223 --> 00:10:24.224
Thanks, Bender.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.311
Dude!

00:10:27.394 --> 00:10:31.440
That herb you scored cleared up
my arthritis and my glaucoma.

00:10:31.523 --> 00:10:32.774
Have you seen Fry?

00:10:32.858 --> 00:10:37.779
Fry? Uh, he, uh, went to get you a burrito
at the gas station.

00:10:37.863 --> 00:10:39.072
Awesome.

00:10:39.156 --> 00:10:42.034
You got to love a dude
that brings the munchie.

00:10:42.117 --> 00:10:45.912
Fry is one guy
I'd definitely never abandon.

00:10:51.877 --> 00:10:53.337
This is my fleam.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.547
You use it to peel the skin
off your enemies

00:10:55.631 --> 00:10:57.674
layer by layer till they die or whatever.

00:10:57.758 --> 00:11:01.011
Neat! Hey, you know
who would love fleaming stuff?

00:11:01.094 --> 00:11:02.721
My friend Bender,

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.182
who I'll never see again.

00:11:05.432 --> 00:11:08.101
Aw, you're homesick, aren't you, T.?

00:11:08.185 --> 00:11:11.605
Mmm-hmm. I miss Earth,
and I'm still hungry.

00:11:11.688 --> 00:11:13.398
Do you have any more of that candy?

00:11:13.482 --> 00:11:15.484
No, but I have a toy Earth.

00:11:18.487 --> 00:11:19.488
Home.

00:11:35.712 --> 00:11:37.839
I didn't abandon you! You wandered off!

00:11:37.923 --> 00:11:39.800
Stop judging me, Fry-bed!

00:11:43.053 --> 00:11:47.099
Oh, it's just not the same
without the muffled screams.

00:11:47.182 --> 00:11:49.601
If only I could hear your voice again.

00:11:52.396 --> 00:11:55.399
Hello, it's me, Fry!
I'm not here right now,

00:11:55.482 --> 00:11:57.859
'cause we're out getting drunk
at the Olive Garden.

00:11:57.943 --> 00:12:02.698
So just leave a message for myself
or Benderafter the tone.See you!

00:12:04.992 --> 00:12:06.076
Aw!

00:12:07.369 --> 00:12:09.037
Fry? Are you home?

00:12:09.121 --> 00:12:12.499
We're supposed to have a date
at the adults-only pancake house.

00:12:12.582 --> 00:12:15.460
Of course he's here
and not on another planet!

00:12:17.421 --> 00:12:21.466
Ooh! In fact,
he's about to talk to you right now.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.135
Oh, good.

00:12:23.677 --> 00:12:25.262
Hello, it's me, Fry.

00:12:25.345 --> 00:12:27.139
I'm... drunk... right now.

00:12:27.723 --> 00:12:28.724
So just leave.

00:12:29.182 --> 00:12:31.643
Okay... I love you.

00:12:32.102 --> 00:12:33.312
Olive... you.

00:12:37.274 --> 00:12:41.278
And finally,
our new employee of the month is Fry.

00:12:41.361 --> 00:12:43.989
He's really been putting
his nose to the grindstone,

00:12:44.072 --> 00:12:46.074
according to Bender's constant updates.

00:12:46.158 --> 00:12:49.369
He's been working so hard,
we barely even see him.

00:12:49.453 --> 00:12:50.996
It's strange, that.

00:12:51.079 --> 00:12:52.497
There's nothing strange about it.

00:12:52.581 --> 00:12:56.043
He's just out of sight
around this corner, exterminating mice.

00:12:57.544 --> 00:12:59.212
Mice... Mice...

00:12:59.296 --> 00:13:00.672
Myself... Elf...

00:13:00.756 --> 00:13:01.882
- Elf.
- Oops.

00:13:02.466 --> 00:13:03.759
Elves are back.

00:13:10.015 --> 00:13:11.308
T. text home?

00:13:11.391 --> 00:13:12.559
Sorry, boy.

00:13:12.643 --> 00:13:15.854
'Cause of the embargo,
our planets aren't allowed to communicate.

00:13:15.938 --> 00:13:17.814
Update Facebook status home?

00:13:19.733 --> 00:13:23.403
Look, my scout manual has a section
on emergency communication.

00:13:23.487 --> 00:13:24.947
Maybe we can rig something up.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.407
Would you like that, boy?
Huh? Would you, boy?

00:13:35.332 --> 00:13:36.333
Watch out!

00:13:36.416 --> 00:13:37.417
Whoa!

00:13:40.337 --> 00:13:43.090
Sorry. This planet has moon problem.

00:13:47.219 --> 00:13:49.346
So what makes this thing fly?

00:13:49.429 --> 00:13:51.139
It's powered by love.

00:13:51.223 --> 00:13:52.975
Aw!

00:13:53.058 --> 00:13:55.477
Okay, stop loving me so much
so we can land.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.561
No problem.

00:14:01.984 --> 00:14:06.530
Okay, this tech dump has every kind of
high-tech communications device.

00:14:06.613 --> 00:14:09.783
Using all of them,
I'm sure I can get a message home.

00:14:12.286 --> 00:14:13.453
There. Finished.

00:14:20.752 --> 00:14:24.089
Oh, God, I can't believe I abandoned Fry.

00:14:24.172 --> 00:14:28.927
I'll never forget the feel of
his soft skin against my flailing fists.

00:14:34.182 --> 00:14:36.310
Oh, wait, there's still some beer left.

00:14:39.062 --> 00:14:40.063
Huh?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.739
"S.O.S."?

00:14:48.822 --> 00:14:50.532
Those are the letters that Fry knows!

00:14:50.616 --> 00:14:52.117
He's alive!

00:14:53.994 --> 00:14:54.995
Yeah?

00:15:00.584 --> 00:15:03.754
Jrrr, how do I watch a funny
on the YouTube?

00:15:03.837 --> 00:15:06.173
It's my dad. Quick, hide!

00:15:10.594 --> 00:15:11.803
What's going on in here?

00:15:11.887 --> 00:15:13.472
Uh, nothing.

00:15:13.555 --> 00:15:16.141
I was just playing foosball. By myself.

00:15:16.224 --> 00:15:18.477
I thought I told you to kill those foos.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.687
Hmm.

00:15:20.771 --> 00:15:24.441
Let's just have a look
in the toy closet, shall we?

00:15:25.859 --> 00:15:27.945
Skull, skull, skull,

00:15:28.028 --> 00:15:29.947
skull, skull... Wait.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.698
Why haven't you fleamed this skull?

00:15:32.074 --> 00:15:34.159
Hi, Mr. Lrrr.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.456
Hey, you're one of those Earth spies
from that Earth ship, aren't you?

00:15:40.123 --> 00:15:41.917
Are you going to kill me?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.502
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:15:44.252 --> 00:15:45.253
Jrrr is.

00:15:47.589 --> 00:15:50.175
Three, two, one...

00:15:56.348 --> 00:15:59.017
Hang on, Fry, I'm a-comin' to save you!

00:16:00.227 --> 00:16:02.354
You are... my... here... o.

00:16:02.437 --> 00:16:04.648
Shut up, Fry, I know it.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:10.821
It's a nice day.

00:16:10.904 --> 00:16:13.365
We'll take him out to the yard,
and after you shoot him,

00:16:13.448 --> 00:16:14.992
we'll play catch with his bladder.

00:16:15.075 --> 00:16:17.244
But I can't. He's my pet.

00:16:17.327 --> 00:16:18.745
You shot your hamster.

00:16:18.829 --> 00:16:20.956
I told you, that was suicide.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.584
He looks kind of sick.

00:16:24.668 --> 00:16:25.669
What have you been feeding him?

00:16:25.752 --> 00:16:27.921
Uh, some stuff I made.

00:16:28.005 --> 00:16:30.882
Whatever. It's time
I made a man out of you.

00:16:30.966 --> 00:16:32.217
Right here, today,

00:16:32.301 --> 00:16:34.803
while I'm not missing anything good on TV.

00:16:34.886 --> 00:16:36.888
Now get in there
and shoot your beloved pet!

00:16:40.767 --> 00:16:42.477
I guess this is good-bye.

00:16:43.979 --> 00:16:45.314
It's okay, Jrrr.

00:16:45.897 --> 00:16:48.108
The week I spent hiding in your closet,

00:16:48.191 --> 00:16:51.194
eating your turds,
was the best week of my life.

00:16:58.785 --> 00:16:59.786
Aah!

00:17:03.832 --> 00:17:05.000
Run, boy! Run!

00:17:13.175 --> 00:17:16.553
He's escaping on a bicycle
powered by love.

00:17:17.137 --> 00:17:19.348
Which is an ordinary thing on this planet.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.358
They're getting away. Love harder!

00:17:29.441 --> 00:17:31.985
We can't, sir.
The men have been hurt too often.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.201
We did it! We're home free!

00:17:39.284 --> 00:17:40.410
Yes, but...

00:17:40.494 --> 00:17:42.120
I'm dying.

00:17:42.579 --> 00:17:44.081
Not 'cause of the turds.

00:17:44.164 --> 00:17:45.290
Can I have a turd?

00:17:45.374 --> 00:17:46.500
Just rest.

00:17:46.583 --> 00:17:48.085
I'm gonna get you to a vet.

00:17:57.052 --> 00:18:00.555
I am Drrr,
doctor of the planet Omicron Persei 8.

00:18:00.639 --> 00:18:03.058
It appears you may have ingested
something toxic.

00:18:03.141 --> 00:18:05.310
Open your mouth and say "Ah!"

00:18:05.394 --> 00:18:07.854
- Ah...
- Good God!

00:18:07.938 --> 00:18:10.565
Here, take some of this herb
to ease the pain.

00:18:11.984 --> 00:18:12.985
Can you save him?

00:18:13.068 --> 00:18:16.196
I could, but he'd only live
another 80 years at most.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.240
The humane thing is to put him to sleep.

00:18:18.865 --> 00:18:19.866
Oh!

00:18:20.534 --> 00:18:22.119
Stop! I won't let you do it!

00:18:23.704 --> 00:18:24.705
Dad?

00:18:24.788 --> 00:18:26.498
Because you have to do it.

00:18:26.581 --> 00:18:29.793
Be a man for once
and fleam this wretched creature.

00:18:29.876 --> 00:18:31.503
I won't.

00:18:32.004 --> 00:18:34.089
I'm not exactly like you, okay?

00:18:34.172 --> 00:18:36.508
I don't want to conquer planets
or kill things,

00:18:36.591 --> 00:18:38.176
or wear a lame cape.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.928
It's not lame, it's lamé.

00:18:40.012 --> 00:18:42.431
And this thing lying on the bed?

00:18:42.514 --> 00:18:45.017
He may be a weird skin ball full of love

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:48.145
and some kind of red juice,
which is delicious, by the way,

00:18:48.228 --> 00:18:49.479
I've been drinking it every day,

00:18:49.563 --> 00:18:50.814
but we're friends.

00:18:50.897 --> 00:18:53.025
And I will not kill him.

00:18:59.698 --> 00:19:00.699
You know,

00:19:00.782 --> 00:19:02.701
standing up to me is pretty manly.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.912
I'll tell you what, sport.
I'll kill him for you.

00:19:05.996 --> 00:19:08.957
Good news!
Nobody has to kill him after all.

00:19:09.041 --> 00:19:10.584
Because he already died!

00:19:12.836 --> 00:19:14.212
T.!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.470
Son...

00:19:21.553 --> 00:19:24.014
I didn't mean it about the cape.

00:19:24.097 --> 00:19:25.432
Capes are cool!

00:19:28.518 --> 00:19:30.687
He's alive.

00:19:30.771 --> 00:19:32.272
At least his butt is.

00:19:38.487 --> 00:19:39.488
Fry?

00:19:40.113 --> 00:19:41.114
Bender.

00:19:41.198 --> 00:19:43.909
I knew you wouldn't abandon me
for much more than a week.

00:19:43.992 --> 00:19:46.370
What's happening? Why is his butt glowing?

00:19:46.453 --> 00:19:48.997
The electromagnetic intensity
of the robot's friendship

00:19:49.081 --> 00:19:52.000
is causing the herbs in his bowels
to bioluminesce with love.

00:19:52.626 --> 00:19:54.586
- Probably.
- That's right, ugly.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.296
I'm here to take my friend home.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.923
Whoa, is that a fleam?

00:19:59.299 --> 00:20:01.510
But, T., can't you stay with me?

00:20:01.593 --> 00:20:03.178
We could grow up together.

00:20:03.261 --> 00:20:06.348
No. I need to grow up on my own planet.

00:20:06.431 --> 00:20:10.018
I must bid you farewell,
my special friend.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.990
What the hell's been going on around here?

00:20:26.952 --> 00:20:28.287
Ah, Fry!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.123
You've been working so hard,
we haven't seen you in days.

00:20:31.206 --> 00:20:32.207
Wait, what?

00:20:32.291 --> 00:20:34.251
No, I was stuck on... Ow!

00:20:34.334 --> 00:20:38.005
Uh, stuck on another delivery
that he undertook on his own.

00:20:38.088 --> 00:20:41.341
We're all very lucky
and not suspicious to have him.

00:20:42.092 --> 00:20:45.345
Hey, Fry, things sure have been
going great between us.

00:20:45.429 --> 00:20:48.098
Remember that make out session
in that dark closet?

00:20:48.181 --> 00:20:49.808
You were like a machine.

00:20:49.891 --> 00:20:51.768
But I...

00:20:51.852 --> 00:20:53.437
Olive... you.

00:20:54.396 --> 00:20:56.023
It's me, Fry!

00:20:56.106 --> 00:20:57.858
It sure is.